In the earlier model in Figure 26, the wire loop rotates and forms a rotor without an iron core;
a stationary permanent magnet establishes the magnetic field.
Rotation changes the magnetic flux through the area enclosed by the loop, inducing an alternating emf.

section_breaks.before:
The stator wire can therefore have an induced emf without moving as the rotating loop does.
Emf depends on the rate of change of flux;
flux that stays constant in time is not enough to induce this emf in a stationary winding.
